{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "dhc:PowerDistributionSystem",
      "message0": "⚡ Power Distribution System %1",
      "args0": [
        { "type": "field_input", "name": "name", "text": "Main Installation" }
      ],
      "message1": "neutral system (régime de neutre) %1",
      "args1": [
        {
          "type": "field_dropdown",
          "name": "neutralSystem",
          "options": [
            ["TT", "TT"],
            ["TN-S", "TN-S"],
            ["TN-C", "TN-C"],
            ["IT", "IT"]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "message2": "medium (electrical system) %1",
      "args2": [
        {
          "type": "field_dropdown",
          "name": "hasMedium",
          "options": [
            ["230 V · 1-phase · 50 Hz", "s223:AC-230VLN-1Ph-50Hz"],
            ["400/230 V · 3-phase · 50 Hz", "s223:AC-400VLL-230VLN-3Ph-50Hz"]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "message3": "① source sub-system — energy generators %1",
      "args3": [
        { "type": "input_statement", "name": "sources", "check": "source" }
      ],
      "message4": "② routing sub-system — inverter & distribution boards %1",
      "args4": [
        { "type": "input_statement", "name": "routes", "check": "route" }
      ],
      "message5": "③ load sub-system — consumers %1",
      "args5": [
        { "type": "input_statement", "name": "sinks", "check": "sink" }
      ],
      "inputsInline": false,
      "colour": "#3b82f6",
      "tooltip": "Root of an electrical installation (dhc:PowerDistributionSystem ⊑ brick:System). It groups three functional sub-systems — sources, routing, sinks — whose members become brick:hasPart on blockly→abox. neutralSystem is the earthing arrangement (régime de neutre); hasMedium (s223:hasMedium) names the electrical system, e.g. s223:AC-230VLN-1Ph-50Hz.",
      "helpUrl": "",
      "data": "dhc:blocklyBlockTemplate=dhc:PowerDistributionSystem"
    },

    {
      "type": "dhc:EnergyDelivery",
      "message0": "🔌 Grid Delivery %1",
      "args0": [
        { "type": "field_input", "name": "name", "text": "Grid" }
      ],
      "message1": "provider %1 · subscribed %2 kVA · %3",
      "args1": [
        { "type": "field_input", "name": "energyProviderName", "text": "Enedis" },
        {
          "type": "field_dropdown",
          "name": "contractedPowerKVA",
          "options": [
            ["3", "3"], ["6", "6"], ["9", "9"], ["12", "12"], ["15", "15"],
            ["18", "18"], ["24", "24"], ["30", "30"], ["36", "36"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "field_dropdown",
          "name": "currentType",
          "options": [
            ["single-phase", "SinglePhase"],
            ["three-phase", "ThreePhase"]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "previousStatement": "source",
      "nextStatement": "source",
      "inputsInline": false,
      "colour": "#3b82f6",
      "tooltip": "The point of supply from the distribution network (dhc:EnergyDelivery). Carries the energy provider, the subscribed / contracted power in kVA (dhc:contractedPowerKVA), and the current type (dhc:currentType). A source member.",
      "helpUrl": "",
      "data": "dhc:blocklyBlockTemplate=dhc:EnergyDelivery"
    },
    {
      "type": "brick:PV_Generation_System",
      "message0": "☀ PV System %1",
      "args0": [
        { "type": "field_input", "name": "name", "text": "Rooftop PV" }
      ],
      "message1": "power %1 kWp",
      "args1": [
        { "type": "field_number", "name": "powerRating", "value": 6, "min": 0, "precision": 0.1 }
      ],
      "previousStatement": "source",
      "nextStatement": "source",
      "inputsInline": false,
      "colour": "#3b82f6",
      "tooltip": "A photovoltaic generation system (brick:PV_Generation_System). powerRating in kWp (dhc:powerRating). A source member.",
      "helpUrl": "",
      "data": "dhc:blocklyBlockTemplate=brick:PV_Generation_System"
    },
    {
      "type": "brick:Battery",
      "message0": "🔋 Battery %1",
      "args0": [
        { "type": "field_input", "name": "name", "text": "Home Battery" }
      ],
      "message1": "power %1 kW",
      "args1": [
        { "type": "field_number", "name": "powerRating", "value": 5, "min": 0, "precision": 0.1 }
      ],
      "previousStatement": "source",
      "nextStatement": "source",
      "inputsInline": false,
      "colour": "#3b82f6",
      "tooltip": "An electrical storage battery (brick:Battery). powerRating in kW (dhc:powerRating). A source member.",
      "helpUrl": "",
      "data": "dhc:blocklyBlockTemplate=brick:Battery"
    },

    {
      "type": "dhc:EnergyMeter",
      "message0": "▭ Energy Meter %1",
      "args0": [
        { "type": "field_input", "name": "name", "text": "Linky" }
      ],
      "previousStatement": "route",
      "nextStatement": "route",
      "inputsInline": false,
      "colour": "#3b82f6",
      "tooltip": "The billing meter at the delivery point, e.g. Linky (dhc:EnergyMeter). A control & routing member.",
      "helpUrl": "",
      "data": "dhc:blocklyBlockTemplate=dhc:EnergyMeter"
    },
    {
      "type": "dhc:EmergencyDisconnect",
      "message0": "⛔ Main Disconnect / AGCP %1",
      "args0": [
        { "type": "field_input", "name": "name", "text": "AGCP" }
      ],
      "message1": "rated %1 A",
      "args1": [
        {
          "type": "field_dropdown",
          "name": "ratedCurrent",
          "options": [["15", "15"], ["30", "30"], ["45", "45"], ["60", "60"], ["63", "63"]]
        }
      ],
      "previousStatement": "route",
      "nextStatement": "route",
      "inputsInline": false,
      "colour": "#3b82f6",
      "tooltip": "The main disconnect at the origin of the installation — the AGCP / disjoncteur d'abonné (dhc:EmergencyDisconnect). ratedCurrent in A (dhc:ratedCurrent). A control & routing member.",
      "helpUrl": "",
      "data": "dhc:blocklyBlockTemplate=dhc:EmergencyDisconnect"
    },
    {
      "type": "dhc:SurgeProtector",
      "message0": "↯ Surge Protector / SPD %1",
      "args0": [
        { "type": "field_input", "name": "name", "text": "Parafoudre" }
      ],
      "previousStatement": "route",
      "nextStatement": "route",
      "inputsInline": false,
      "colour": "#3b82f6",
      "tooltip": "A Surge Protective Device / parafoudre (dhc:SurgeProtector), mandatory per NF C 15-100 §443. A control & routing member; typically at the main board.",
      "helpUrl": "",
      "data": "dhc:blocklyBlockTemplate=dhc:SurgeProtector"
    },
    {
      "type": "brick:Inverter",
      "message0": "⇄ Inverter %1",
      "args0": [
        { "type": "field_input", "name": "name", "text": "Hybrid Inverter" }
      ],
      "message1": "power %1 kW",
      "args1": [
        { "type": "field_number", "name": "powerRating", "value": 6, "min": 0, "precision": 0.1 }
      ],
      "previousStatement": "route",
      "nextStatement": "route",
      "inputsInline": false,
      "colour": "#3b82f6",
      "tooltip": "Converts and routes energy between sources and the board (brick:Inverter). powerRating in kW (dhc:powerRating). A control & routing member.",
      "helpUrl": "",
      "data": "dhc:blocklyBlockTemplate=brick:Inverter"
    },
    {
      "type": "dhc:DistributionBoard",
      "message0": "▦ Main Distribution Board %1",
      "args0": [
        { "type": "field_input", "name": "name", "text": "Main Board" }
      ],
      "mutator": "dhc_board_mutator",
      "previousStatement": "route",
      "nextStatement": "route",
      "inputsInline": false,
      "colour": "#3b82f6",
      "tooltip": "The main consumer unit (dhc:DistributionBoard). A control & routing member. Use the ⚙ gear to add/remove rows (DIN rails); each rail holds circuit definitions and protection modules.",
      "helpUrl": "",
      "data": "dhc:blocklyBlockTemplate=dhc:DistributionBoard"
    },

    {
      "type": "dhc:Circuit",
      "message0": "● Circuit %1",
      "args0": [
        { "type": "field_input", "name": "name", "text": "Circuit" }
      ],
      "message1": "line %1",
      "args1": [
        { "type": "field_variable", "name": "CIRCUIT_VAR", "variable": "CB_Circuit", "variableTypes": ["Circuit"], "defaultType": "Circuit" }
      ],
      "message2": "type %1 · %2 A · %3 mm²",
      "args2": [
        {
          "type": "field_dropdown",
          "name": "hasCircuitType",
          "options": [
            ["Lighting", "dhc:CircuitType_Lighting"],
            ["Socket", "dhc:CircuitType_Socket"],
            ["Cooking", "dhc:CircuitType_Cooking"],
            ["Dedicated appliance", "dhc:CircuitType_DedicatedAppliance"],
            ["Water heater", "dhc:CircuitType_WaterHeater"],
            ["Heating", "dhc:CircuitType_Heating"],
            ["Floor heating", "dhc:CircuitType_FloorHeating"],
            ["IRVE (EV)", "dhc:CircuitType_IRVE"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "field_dropdown",
          "name": "ratedCurrent",
          "options": [["6", "6"], ["10", "10"], ["16", "16"], ["20", "20"], ["25", "25"], ["32", "32"], ["40", "40"], ["63", "63"]]
        },
        {
          "type": "field_dropdown",
          "name": "crossSection",
          "options": [["1.5", "1.5"], ["2.5", "2.5"], ["4", "4"], ["6", "6"], ["10", "10"], ["16", "16"]]
        }
      ],
      "message3": "%1-phase · protection %2",
      "args3": [
        { "type": "field_dropdown", "name": "phase", "options": [["1", "1"], ["3", "3"]] },
        { "type": "field_dropdown", "name": "protection", "options": [["MCB (needs a differential)", "MCB"], ["RCBO (integral differential)", "RCBO"]] }
      ],
      "message4": "differential %1",
      "args4": [
        { "type": "field_variable", "name": "DIFFERENTIAL", "variable": "ID_Main", "variableTypes": ["Differential"], "defaultType": "Differential" }
      ],
      "message5": "max points %1 · dedicated %2",
      "args5": [
        { "type": "field_number", "name": "maxPoints", "value": 8, "min": 0, "precision": 1 },
        { "type": "field_checkbox", "name": "dedicated", "checked": false }
      ],
      "previousStatement": "module",
      "nextStatement": "module",
      "inputsInline": false,
      "colour": "#3b82f6",
      "tooltip": "A protected line (dhc:Circuit) — the unit the C-Box validates. Sits on a board rail. Its `line` variable is the token loads reference via 'protected by'. The `differential` variable references the dhc:RCD device protecting it — SHARED referencing is how the topology is expressed: all circuits → one differential = one-per-install (older NF C 15-100); one differential per rail = one-per-rail (newer editions). An RCBO circuit is its own differential (protection = RCBO). On blockly→abox it becomes dhc:Circuit + dhc:hasProtection (its breaker + the referenced RCD) + dhc:hasWiring.",
      "helpUrl": "",
      "data": "dhc:blocklyBlockTemplate=dhc:Circuit"
    },
    {
      "type": "dhc:RCD",
      "message0": "⧉ RCD / differential %1",
      "args0": [
        { "type": "field_input", "name": "name", "text": "Main differential" }
      ],
      "message1": "id %1",
      "args1": [
        { "type": "field_variable", "name": "RCD_VAR", "variable": "ID_Main", "variableTypes": ["Differential"], "defaultType": "Differential" }
      ],
      "message2": "type %1 · %2 mA · rated %3 A",
      "args2": [
        { "type": "field_dropdown", "name": "rcdType", "options": [["AC", "AC"], ["A", "A"], ["B", "B"], ["F", "F"]] },
        { "type": "field_dropdown", "name": "sensitivityMA", "options": [["30", "30"], ["300", "300"]] },
        { "type": "field_dropdown", "name": "ratedCurrent", "options": [["25", "25"], ["40", "40"], ["63", "63"], ["80", "80"]] }
      ],
      "previousStatement": "module",
      "nextStatement": "module",
      "inputsInline": false,
      "colour": "#3b82f6",
      "tooltip": "A differential device (dhc:RCD) — this is where the differential is DEFINED (rcdType, sensitivityMA, ratedCurrent). Its `id` variable is the token circuits reference via 'differential'. Drop ONE and have every circuit reference it for one-per-install (older norm); drop one per rail and reference it from that rail's circuits for one-per-rail (newer norm). A DIN-rail module.",
      "helpUrl": "",
      "data": "dhc:blocklyBlockTemplate=dhc:RCD"
    },

    {
      "type": "dhc:Socket",
      "message0": "◵ Socket %1",
      "args0": [
        { "type": "field_input", "name": "name", "text": "Socket" }
      ],
      "message1": "protected by %1",
      "args1": [
        { "type": "field_variable", "name": "FED_BY", "variable": "CB_Circuit", "variableTypes": ["Circuit"], "defaultType": "Circuit" }
